timestamp=2026-11-04T19:18:13.411Z level=INFO run=c2c30b4a message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Hmm, billing cycle every week? Or maybe the billing period for each \"month\" is the group of entries that belong to that billing month's cycle.\n# Another reading: \"For each month, the billing period for all employees starts on the same day of the week inherited from the dataset's earliest record.\n# On that day, employees are required to appear at the workplace to collect their salary.\"\n# So each calendar month has a billing period starting on that weekday. For example, in March 2025, find the Tuesday (weekday inherited) that is the start of billing period for March?\n# Maybe the first Tuesday of the calendar month, or the Tuesday closest to month start? Or perhaps the billing period for March is the interval starting on the Tuesday that falls in March?\n# Or could be that the \"monthly\" is by calendar month (Mar, Apr, etc), and the \"billing period starts on same day of week\" is just context about when salary is collected - maybe the week day doesn't affect the grouping, just operational detail?\n# But it says \"monthly salary for each employee for every month\". Also \"For each month...\" - probably calendar month. Let us look at the numbers more. Also check the actual expected grouping by looking at typical contest datasets? Or infer from totals?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
